,"source-block-1297","Launchpad/Custom/Available/2-MF-Presets",["Updated","making music","launchpad"]],["2026-11-28%20Sat/","source-block-1346","Launchpad/Custom/Available/3-MF-Number-Pad",["Updated","making music","launchpad"]],["2026-11-28%20Sat/","source-block-1398","Launchpad/Custom/Slot/8",["Updated","making music","launchpad"]],["2026-11-28%20Sat/","source-block-1431","Launchpad/Q/Can-Custom-Mode-select-MicroFreak-presets-by-bank-and-program-change",["Updated","making music","launchpad"]],["2026-11-28%20Sat/","source-block-1521","midi",["Updated","making music"]],["2026-11-28%20Sat/","source-block-1530","MIDI",["Updated","making music","midi"]],["2026-11-28%20Sat/","source-block-1544","MIDI/CC",["Updated","making music","midi"]],["2026-11-28%20Sat/","source-block-1561","MIDI/Message",["Updated","making music","midi"]],["2026-11-28%20Sat/","source-block-1583","MIDI/Pitch-Bend",["Updated","making music","midi"]],["2026-11-28%20Sat/","source-block-1608","MIDI/Program-Change",["Updated","making music","midi"]],["2026-11-28%20Sat/","source-block-1637","MIDI/Q/Which-MIDI-CC-numbers-are-free-for-custom-mappings",["Updated","making music","midi"]],["2026-11-28%20Sat/","source-block-1704","MIDI/SysEx",["Updated","making music","midi"]],["A11y/WCAG/","source-block-34","Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) international standard",[]],["A2A/","source-block-88","A2A",[]],["A2A/","source-block-125","Overview",["A2A"]],["A2A/","source-block-140","Agent2Agent (A2A) is an open protocol for communication and interoperability between opaque agentic applications: agents built on different frameworks, by different vendors, on separate servers, collaborate as agents without exposing their internal state, memory, or tools.",["A2A","Overview"]],["A2A/","source-block-424","Created by Google and contributed as an open source project under the Linux Foundation; Apache 2.0 licensed. In August 2026 it was accepted as a Growth Stage project of the Linux Foundation-directed Agentic AI Foundation (AAIF), alongside MCP, goose, and AGENTS.md. (announcement)",["A2A","Overview"]],["A2A/","source-block-798","Normative links",["A2A"]],["A2A/","source-block-820","A2A Protocol Specification — latest released spec version 1.0.0; earlier versions 0.3.0, 0.2.6, 0.1.0",["A2A","Normative links"]],["A2A/","source-block-986","a2aproject/A2A — spec repo; latest release v1.0.1 (2026-05-28), v1.0.0 released 2026-03-12",["A2A","Normative links"]],["A2A/","source-block-1177","Scope",["A2A"]],["A2A/","source-block-1189","Agent Card — JSON metadata an A2A server publishes describing identity, capabilities, skills, service endpoint, and auth requirements; discovered at /.well-known/agent-card.json, via registries, or by direct configuration.",["A2A","Scope"]],["A2A/","source-block-1424","Task — the stateful unit of work with a defined lifecycle; Message — a turn with role user or agent made of Parts (text, file references, structured data); Artifact — a task output made of Parts.",["A2A","Scope"]],["A2A/","source-block-1650","Interaction modes: synchronous request/response, streaming over Server-Sent Events, and asynchronous push notifications to a client webhook for long-running tasks.",["A2A","Scope"]],["A2A/","source-block-1818","The spec is layered: a canonical data model (Protocol Buffer messages), abstract operations (send message, send streaming message, get / list / cancel task, get Agent Card), and protocol bindings for JSON-RPC 2.0, gRPC, and HTTP+JSON/REST, plus custom bindings.",["A2A","Scope"]],["A2A/","source-block-2084","Relationship to MCP",["A2A"]],["A2A/","source-block-2110","MCP connects an agent to tools and resources (vertical: deepens one agent); A2A connects agents to other agents across team or organization boundaries (horizontal). The two are designed as complements. (A2A and MCP)",["A2A","Relationship to MCP"]],["A2A/","source-block-2389","Implementations",["A2A"]],["A2A/","source-block-2411","Official SDKs for Python (a2a-sdk), Go, JavaScript, Java, .NET, and Rust, linked from the spec repo README.",["A2A","Implementations"]],["A2A/","source-block-2525","LangSmith Agent Server exposes each assistant at /a2a/{assistant_id} (methods message/send, message/stream, tasks/get) and serves its Agent Card at /.well-known/agent-card.json?assistant_id={assistant_id}. (A2A endpoint in Agent Server)",["A2A","Implementations"]],["A2A/","source-block-2831","A LangSmith Deployment of a LangSmith/Deep Agents agent can expose it via MCP or A2A. (Going to production)",["A2A","Implementations"]],["Abbreviation/","source-block-66","An abbreviation shortens a word or phrase (e.g., Dr., etc., UN).",[]],["AbleSet/","source-block-88","AbleSet",[]],["AbleSet/","source-block-124","Setlist manager for Ableton/Live performances. Its site describes it as \"the easiest way to manage and control your Ableton Live Set.\"",["AbleSet"]],["AbleSet/","source-block-266","Builds the setlist from the Live set's locators. Songs can be reordered, colored and annotated from a browser on any device on the same local network, without an internet connection.",["AbleSet"]],["AbleSet/","source-block-452","Shows synced lyrics and chords on those devices. Lyrics live in the Live set as a MIDI track named with +LYRICS, one clip per line, with the line's text as the clip name (lyrics docs). Generators build that track from pasted lyrics or an .lrc file.",["AbleSet"]],["AbleSet/","source-block-744","Paid. Intro ($129), Standard ($179) and Pro ($269) were listed on 2026-10-10 Sat. Intro shows one lyrics track; Standard and Pro show any number. The free trial stops playback every 15 minutes.",["AbleSet"]],["AbleSet/","source-block-945","Built on Person/Leo Bernard/GitHub/ableton-js.",["AbleSet"]],["Ableton/","source-block-0","Ableton/Manual",[]],["Ableton/","block-64567962-d010-470d-8d63-fec17ad76184","Quantizing",["Ableton/Manual"]],["Ableton/","source-block-245","10.4.7 Quantizing Notes",["Ableton/Manual","Quantizing"]],["Ableton/","source-block-318","Quantize: [CMD][U]",["Ableton/Manual","Quantizing"]],["Ableton/","source-block-342","Quantize Settings... [CTRL][Shift][U] [CMD][Shift][U]",["Ableton/Manual","Quantizing"]],["Ableton/","source-block-446","You can make the grid expand or contract with CMD[1-2]",["Ableton/Manual","Quantizing"]],["Ableton/","source-block-736","CMD+6 is sixteenth note",["Ableton/Manual","Quantizing"]],["Ableton/","source-block-765","CMD+7 is 8th note",["Ableton/Manual","Quantizing"]],["Ableton/","source-block-788","CMD+8 is quarter note",["Ableton/Manual","Quantizing"]],["Ableton/","source-block-815","CMD+9 is 1-bar",["Ableton/Manual","Quantizing"]],["Ableton/","source-block-835","CMD+0 is off",["Ableton/Manual","Quantizing"]],["Ableton/Arrangement%20View/Clip/How%20To/Play%20in%20a%20loop/","source-block-41","How to play a section of the arrangement view in a loop",[]],["Ableton/Arrangement%20View/Clip/How%20To/Play%20in%20a%20loop/","source-block-101","Steps",["How to play a section of the arrangement view in a loop"]],["Ableton/Arrangement%20View/Clip/How%20To/Play%20in%20a%20loop/","source-block-113","Make a time selection over the part of the clip you want to hear (even if it's in the middle of a clip).",["How to play a section of the arrangement view in a loop","Steps"]],["Ableton/Arrangement%20View/Clip/How%20To/Play%20in%20a%20loop/","source-block-226","See also Ableton/Arrangement View/Clip/How To/Select in a not quantized way if that's desired",["How to play a section of the arrangement view in a loop","Steps","Make a time selection over the part of the clip you want to hear (even if it's in the middle of a clip)."]],["Ableton/Arrangement%20View/Clip/How%20To/Play%20in%20a%20loop/","source-block-329","Right-click the top timeline or the selection and choose:",["How to play a section of the arrangement view in a loop","Steps"]]],"format_version":5}